<title>UK: Burton 18 weeks turnover up 9.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Burton 18 weeks turnover up 9.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retail group Burton Group Plc said on Tuesday that turnover for the 18 weeks to July 4 was up 9.7 percent.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that turnover at Debenhams, which it plans to demerge, was up 14.2 percent. Excluding home shopping, sales were up 10.4 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Trading is in line with expectations, costs are well under control and, despite the difficult weather in June, the group remains confident for the balance of the year,&quot; said the company.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
